.SH NAME
firmware \- a logical object definition in the xCAT database.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBfirmware Attributes:\fR  \fIcfgfile\fR, \fIcomments\fR, \fIdisable\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Logical objects of this type are stored in the xCAT database in one or more tables.  Use the following commands
to manipulate the objects: \fBmkdef\fR, \fBchdef\fR, \fBlsdef\fR, and \fBrmdef\fR.  These commands will take care of
knowing which tables the object attributes should be stored in.  The attribute list below shows, in
parentheses, what tables each attribute is stored in.
.SH "firmware Attributes:"
.IX Header "firmware Attributes:"
.IP "\fBcfgfile\fR (firmware.cfgfile)" 6
.IX Item "cfgfile (firmware.cfgfile)"
The file to use.
.IP "\fBcomments\fR (firmware.comments)" 6
.IX Item "comments (firmware.comments)"
Any user-written notes.
.IP "\fBdisable\fR (firmware.disable)" 6
.IX Item "disable (firmware.disable)"
Set to 'yes' or '1' to comment out this row.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
